cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these anchors, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "COCO-WholeBody keypoint anchors for the ANNY base mesh"
authors:
  - name: "weft"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
abstract: >-
  Vertex-weight anchors that place COCO-WholeBody keypoints on ANNY's 19,158-vertex
  makehuman base mesh, in the format anny.keypoints.KeypointsRegressor.load_precomputed
  reads: label -> per-vertex regression weights summing to one.

  65 of the 133 labels carry weights. Indices 0 to 22, the body and the feet, are copied
  by name from ANNY's own coco.pth, which ships exactly those 23. Indices 91 to 132, the
  42 hand points, are built here from the rig's skinning weights and the mesh: three
  phalanx heads per digit, and a fingertip taken as the furthest skinned vertex along the
  digit's own axis, because a tip is the far end of the last bone rather than a joint and
  template_bone_tails is None on this topology. Median blend spread is 7.8 mm, about a
  pencil; the widest is 18.1 mm at the thumb base, about a AA battery.

  The 68 face landmarks, indices 23 to 90, have no weights. They are named in
  wholebody133.json as missing rather than filled with a guess. ANNY has no facial action
  bones -- its 104 bones include only neck01 to neck03, head, eye.L and eye.R -- so they
  need vertex correspondence against the hm08 topology, which is separate work.

  The copy from coco.pth is keyed by label and not by position, because the two orders
  differ: ANNY stores left_big_toe, right_big_toe, left_small_toe, ... while
  COCO-WholeBody indices 17 to 22 are left_big_toe, left_small_toe, left_heel, right_...
  A copy by slice puts four of six foot points on the wrong point, and nothing raises.
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Anny"
    authors:
      - name: "NAVER Corp."
    url: "https://github.com/naver/anny"
    license: Apache-2.0
  - type: software
    title: "MMPose"
    authors:
      - name: "MMPose Contributors"
    url: "https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmpose"
    notes: >-
      configs/_base_/datasets/coco_wholebody.py is the published index order this
      repository is checked against.
